# Scheduled jobs for KAI.
#
# Install with:
#
#   crontab deploy/scheduler/kai.cron
#
# or, to keep it out of the user crontab entirely:
#
#   sudo install -m 0644 deploy/scheduler/kai.cron /etc/cron.d/kai
#
# Check it loaded, without installing:
#
#   crontab deploy/scheduler/kai.cron -l
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Timezone
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRON_TZ is honoured by Vixie cron, Debian/Ubuntu cron and cronie. It is NOT
# honoured by busybox crond, which is what Alpine and most container base
# images ship. The line below is therefore documentation-first: if your cron
# ignores it, the schedule still runs every 15 minutes, just not aligned to UTC.
#
# That degradation is bounded and is the reason this job is specified at a 15
# minute cadence rather than a fixed wall-clock time. Every real-world UTC
# offset is a whole number of quarter-hours, so `*/15 * * * *` fires exactly
# every 15 minutes in any timezone. Only the phase against absolute UTC moves.
# The purge itself is timezone-independent: it deletes on `expires_at <= now()`
# against a `timestamptz` column, so no run depends on the host clock's zone.
#
# Every timezone-named zone below is set for the *command environment* as well,
# so the timestamps the job logs are UTC regardless of what the scheduler does
# with CRON_TZ.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

#: Where this repository is checked out. Change this one line.
KAI_HOME=/opt/kai

#: The Compose project the deployment runs under. The purge must reach the same
#: database as the running app; a mismatch here creates a second, empty stack
#: that purges nothing and looks like it worked.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=kai

#: Set once per run rather than exported globally, so `docker compose` picks up
#: the deployment's .env (its real secrets) without this file containing any.
#: Every run is also timed out, so a wedged database cannot overlap the next one.
*/15 * * * * TZ=UTC KAI_COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME cd $KAI_HOME && TZ=UTC ./deploy/scheduler/run-purge-revocations.sh >> $KAI_HOME/var/purge-scheduler.log 2>&1
